/T (The term "ribbon" refers to the region at the top of the application that houses the MS Excel toolbars and menu items. With CTRL+F1, the ribbon can be displayed or hidden. The toolbars and menus have been replaced by the ribbon, which runs across the application's top. The top of the ribbons has a number of tabs, and each tab has its own set of commands. It has numerous tabs, including File, Home, View, Insert, and others. The ribbon can be altered to fit your requirements. Right-click on the Ribbon and choose "Customise the Ribbon" from the menu that appears. The following window appears as shown below. Each of these options is available for you to select or deselect.)
